{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimensionBinder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimensionBinder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.exists_realised_not_central_at_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.exists_realised_not_central_at_three","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L160-L168","doc":"**The threshold is real.** At `d = 3` there is a realised surface holonomy\nthat is *not* central, so `mass_central_of_closed` cannot be extended past the\nthreshold and its dimension hypothesis is not removable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.not_mem_center_of_noncomm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.not_mem_center_of_noncomm","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L154-L158","doc":"An element failing to commute with something is not central. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.stratumThree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.stratumThree","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L146-L152","doc":"A stratum at `d = 3`, realising everything. The Stokes field is discharged\nbecause its hypothesis is false at this dimension: a boundary *is* available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.adjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.adjoint","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L138-L144","doc":"Any group is a crossed module over itself, with the identity feedback and\nconjugation as the twisting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.mass_central_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.mass_central_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L128-L131","doc":"The dimension-1 rung. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.mass_central_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.mass_central_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L123-L126","doc":"The dimension-2 rung, as a value of the family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.mass_central_of_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.mass_central_of_closed","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L111-L121","doc":"**Below the threshold the mass is central.** At a stratum whose dimension\nleaves no room for a boundary, every realised surface holonomy is central, so\nthe mass is an abelian invariant.\n\nThe conclusion is *derived*: the Stokes field supplies `Φ h = 1`, and\n`ker_le_center` — which is proved from the Peiffer identity, not assumed —\ncarries it to centrality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.feedback_trivial_of_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.feedback_trivial_of_closed","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L106-L106","doc":"2-dimensional Stokes at a boundaryless stratum (ASSUMED, not proved). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.realised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.realised","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The surface holonomies this stratum realises. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.d","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The spatial dimension of the base. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.C","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The crossed module of the stratum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.DescentStratum","kind":"structure","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L91-L107","doc":"A rung of the descent ladder at spatial dimension `d`.\n\n`realised` is the set of surface holonomies the stratum actually produces, and\n`feedback_trivial_of_closed` is the 2-dimensional Stokes theorem as it bears on\nthis rung: at a dimension with no boundary available, a realised surface\nholonomy has trivial feedback image. That field is an **assumption** — the\ncorpus cites Yekutieli for it and does not prove it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.not_boundaryAvailable_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.not_boundaryAvailable_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L88-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.not_boundaryAvailable_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.not_boundaryAvailable_one","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L85-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.not_boundaryAvailable_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.not_boundaryAvailable_two","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L82-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.boundaryAvailable_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.boundaryAvailable_three","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L79-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.boundaryAvailable_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.boundaryAvailable_iff","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L73-L77","doc":"The threshold, in the form the descent ladder uses it: a boundary is\navailable exactly from dimension three up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.BoundaryAvailable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.BoundaryAvailable","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L68-L71","doc":"`Σ` can be a **proper** submanifold of the base, hence can carry a non-empty\nboundary, exactly when the ambient dimension strictly exceeds its own. At or\nbelow that, `Σ` is forced to be the whole base (closed) or to degenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.massSurfaceDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.SpatialDimension.massSurfaceDim","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/SpatialDimensionBinder.lean#L64-L66","doc":"The mass identity's surface `Σ` is two-dimensional: the multiplicative\nintegral of `def:mass-identity` is the 2-dimensional one. ","signatureChunk":0}]}